capability ldap/filter-parse  a search filter (RFC 4515) read from text into a value, every escape
  heroes  ldap.parse_filter, ldap.Filter, ldap.MAX_FILTER_DEPTH
  java    DirContext.search (a filter as text), InvalidSearchFilterException
  dotnet  SearchRequest.Filter (as text)
  go      CompileFilter
  rust    -
  python  Connection.search (search_filter as text)
  note    RFC 4515's grammar: `((cn=a))`, `(cn=a**b)`, `(cn=a(b)`, `(=a)` and `(:=x)` refused where Go reads them; `:DN` read as dnAttributes, ABNF's strings being blind to case, where Go reads a rule named DN; the parentheses around the whole may be left out, where Go asks for them

capability ldap/filter-format  a filter value written back as RFC 4515's text
  heroes  ldap.format_filter
  java    -
  dotnet  -
  go      DecompileFilter
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    a value that is UTF-8 kept as text, where Go's `DecompileFilter` escapes every byte past ASCII

capability ldap/filter-escape  a value escaped to stand inside a filter's text, and unescaped
  heroes  ldap.escape_filter, ldap.escape_filter_bytes, ldap.unescape_filter
  java    -
  dotnet  -
  go      EscapeFilter
  rust    -
  python  utils.conv.escape_filter_chars, utils.conv.escape_bytes, utils.conv.unescape_filter_chars, utils.conv.is_filter_escaped, utils.conv.ldap_escape_to_bytes
  note    `escape_filter` keeps characters past ASCII, as Python's `escape_filter_chars` does; `escape_filter_bytes` escapes them, as Go's `EscapeFilter` does

capability ldap/filter-ber  a filter written as BER and read back from it
